<DataObject xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns="http://sifassociation.org/SpecGen" name="StudentParticipation">
  <Key>@RefId</Key>
  <EventsReported>true</EventsReported>
  <Item>
    <Element>StudentParticipation</Element>
    <Description>
      <p>
        The <code>StudentParticipation</code> object represents a student's participation in a specific program, service, or initiative over a defined
        period of time. Each instance links a single student to a single program and may include identifiers, participation status, entry and exit dates,
        and other program-specific characteristics required for exchange, reporting, and auditing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Multiple <code>StudentParticipation</code> instances may exist for the same student in order to represent participation in multiple programs,
        concurrent enrollments, or successive periods of participation in the same program. Implementations may use <code>StudentParticipation</code>
        as the primary representation of program membership or in conjunction with program-related elements in <code>StudentPersonal</code>, provided
        that the authoritative source and synchronization rules for each program are clearly defined.
      </p>
      <p>
        See the <code>StudentPersonal</code> description for details on when to use which type of object for program membership.
      </p>
    </Description>
  </Item>
